{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SIGNING BUG PROVEN AND FILED: a83f-6348-a08c-401d (georgiaite-flawless-sawfish, p1, open), discovered_from 2ddd, caused_by d70a-d06e-aea0-4008. Root cause proven by hermetic experiment, NOT inference: sign_manifest validates against store-wide tracker HEAD rather than the subject's own generation, at THREE sites - generation.py:292 before/after fence; generation.py:335 under-lock check that is anti-correlated by construction (a process only moves HEAD by committing under that lock, so a blocked acquisition ends just after a HEAD-moving commit); relation_snapshot.py:145 unlocked git status hitting the writer's add->commit gap (58.4% probe failure). Median inter-commit gap on the tracker is 3s and 65 of the last 120 commits are rebar's OWN background enrichment, while collect() takes 3.3-3.7s - so with MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS=3, no backoff and no jitter, the recovery is structurally unable to succeed. CORRECTS MY EARLIER CLAIM that the churn was partly self-inflicted by my ticket edits: it is dominated by rebar's own machinery. The guarding regression test (test_plan_review_generation_scope.py:41, titled 'Signing must survive UNRELATED concurrent tracker writes') monkeypatches tracker_head_sha to a constant so it can never observe the fence firing - the same green-but-vacuous oracle class that sibling ticket d075 exists to catch."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787371701294154001,"uuid":"52f8d7b2-2dfc-4176-88e9-91d181124ab7"}